  passage: "Software maintenance is the process of modifying a software system after delivery. Four types of maintenance are recognized: corrective, adaptive, perfective and preventive. <b>(71)</b> maintenance fixes errors discovered after delivery. <b>(72)</b> maintenance adapts the software to a changed environment, such as a new operating system or new hardware. Most maintenance effort, however, is spent on <b>(73)</b> maintenance, which provides enhancements and new features for users. To reduce future maintenance cost, designers should aim for high <b>(74)</b> — the ease with which a software system can be modified. Good documentation, modular design and thorough <b>(75)</b> all contribute to easier maintenance."
